European leaders have agreed to nominate the former head of the Bank of Spain as the next president of the European Central Bank. Pablo ​Hernandez ‌de ⁠Cos will replace the outgoing Christine Lagarde as the bank faces pressure to tackle high inflation, borrowing costs, and government debt. Also in the show - US regulators give SpaceX the green light to send satellites for data centers into space, and American households face higher costs for their Thanksgiving celebrations. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2393400-e9e0-11f1-93c6-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-10efea26.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2393400-e9e0-11f1-93c6-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-10efea26.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dfdafcb0-e9dd-11f1-a46c-d51594891b98</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:40:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Kate MOODY</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Nigeria faces rising election violence in run up to vote</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nigeria-faces-rising-election-violence-in-run-up-to-vote</link><description>
In tonight's edition,  concerns are mounting that electoral violence could deter voters from taking part in Nigeria’s presidential election in January. Also, the driver of a car suspected of causing a fuel tanker to overturn on a major highway in Egypt is detained. And Sierra Leone was once considered the most dangerous place in the world to give birth. Today, maternal deaths have dropped dramatically.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1dcc0b04-e9de-11f1-b26d-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/DL00006218-VOD-00023675-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1dcc0b04-e9de-11f1-b26d-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/DL00006218-VOD-00023675-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">92e6ded2-e9de-11f1-813e-59c451a64275</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:21:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Iranian monarchists disrupt Paris event, highlighting bitter diaspora divide</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261126-iranian-monarchists-disrupt-paris-event-highlighting-bitter-diaspora-divide</link><description>
A Paris event on Iranian women's rights attended by French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot was disrupted when diaspora supporters of Reza Pahlavi, the US-based son of Iran's deposed shah, taunted left-leaning opponents of Iran's Islamic regime. The chaos underscored the bitter divides in the Iranian diaspora as the Iran war enters its tenth month.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e1a9d64-e9d5-11f1-a648-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/ima-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e1a9d64-e9d5-11f1-a648-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/ima-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">39aa9754-e9d5-11f1-8be4-0fdcb9591f43</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:09:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e1a9d64-e9d5-11f1-a648-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/ima-2.jpg">© Screengrab X</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Sanchez's big gamble: Will Spain swing from Socialists to hard right?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261126-sanchez-s-big-gamble-will-spain-swing-from-socialists-to-hard-right</link><description>
For eight years, he’s been a mainstay among European leaders, one who’s snatched victory from the jaws of defeat before but has Pedro Sanchez run out of road this time? Spain's Socialist prime minister dogged by incumbent fatigue and nepotism allegations. Sanchez gambled on turning the rift in his coalition over his country's housing shortage into a referendum on his country's strong growth and calling a snap general election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd2c626e-e9cb-11f1-a182-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T191001Z-29917429-RC27VOA4BVBZ-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-ELECTION-PP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd2c626e-e9cb-11f1-a182-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T191001Z-29917429-RC27VOA4BVBZ-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-ELECTION-PP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7d701670-e9c7-11f1-bdb1-23595fa0119e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:53:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hamas weighs response after Israel kills 10 people in Gaza</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/hamas-weighs-response-after-israel-kills-10-people-in-gaza</link><description>
Five Israeli strikes and a shooting overnight and on Thursday killed 10 Palestinians across Gaza, according to officials at Shifa and Al-Aqsa Martyrs hospitals, where the casualties were taken. A strike on a residential apartment in Deir Al-Balah in central Gaza killed a man and his wife, the officials said. FRANCE 24's Jennie Shin speaks with journalist Ahmed Dremly, who was in Gaza until six months ago and has extensively covered the humanitarian crisis there.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4351c01e-e9d7-11f1-a478-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-210731-211826-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4351c01e-e9d7-11f1-a478-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-210731-211826-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48ad2918-e9d7-11f1-ab34-f19fc60df09a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:35:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump urges Putin to end 'military aggression' in Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-urges-putin-to-end-military-aggression-in-europe</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said Thursday he had asked Vladimir Putin to "pull back all military aggression" against Europe, in a shift in tone towards the leader Russian he called his friend just a week ago. Trump said he had made the request to Putin when they met in China last week, adding that he thought it would help lead to a deal to end Moscow's grinding war in Ukraine. The US leader's comments come a day after he hosted NATO chief Mark Rutte in Florida, after which they issued a joint statement calling on Russia not to expand the Ukraine war. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6c3707a-e9d4-11f1-8cb6-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-200333-200843-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6c3707a-e9d4-11f1-8cb6-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-200333-200843-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dbdd4d2e-e9d4-11f1-8be7-516fc2299180</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:10:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France's Bardella faces new allegations of anti-Semitic comments</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-bardella-faces-new-allegations-of-antisemitic-comments</link><description>
French far-right leader Jordan Bardella on Thursday faced new accusations of having made anti-Semitic remarks as a teenager, after French media published extracts from previously unaired conversations online. The 31-year-old top ally of French presidential candidate Marine Le Pen has denied any wrongdoing after allegations emerged in September that he made conspiracist comments about Jewish people on Facebook in 2013. FRANCE 24's Solange Mougin reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bfd8a0a-e9d4-11f1-91c4-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-201404-201552-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bfd8a0a-e9d4-11f1-91c4-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-201404-201552-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">214b5910-e9d4-11f1-aa9f-dd9b20d60625</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:05:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Le Pen slams push for EU budget deal before French election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/le-pen-slams-push-for-eu-budget-deal-before-french-election</link><description>
EU leaders locked horns over the bloc's budget at a summit meeting in Brussels on Thursday, as far-right leader Marine Le Pen slammed an "underhanded" push to lock in the long-term spending plans before French presidential elections next year. European Council head Antonio Costa turned up the pressure upon arrival at the budget talks, where heavyweight Germany is pressing for cuts as well as burden-sharing on money for Ukraine. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2c2241c-e9d2-11f1-a270-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-200845-201341-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2c2241c-e9d2-11f1-a270-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-200845-201341-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a7a2cb26-e9d2-11f1-83e2-f598b54f400c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:02:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Marie-Antoinette’s porcelain ‘nipple bowl’ fetches record $3.1 million at Paris auction</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261126-marie-antoinette-s-porcelain-nipple-bowl-fetches-record-3-1-million-at-paris-auction</link><description>
A "jatte-teton", or nipple bowl, that once belonged to French Queen Marie-Antoinette fetched a record €2.9 million ($3.1 million) at Paris auction Thursday. The breast-shaped porcelain bowl was one of four such pieces which King Louis XVI once ordered for his queen's royal dairy creamery.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/754a8f7e-e9d2-11f1-8d65-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/78094fe8091a889d987d8404140ef255ffd47c89.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/754a8f7e-e9d2-11f1-8d65-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/78094fe8091a889d987d8404140ef255ffd47c89.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">762d9918-e9d2-11f1-acc4-2108a1abf8ad</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:49:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/754a8f7e-e9d2-11f1-8d65-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/78094fe8091a889d987d8404140ef255ffd47c89.jpg">© Dimitar Dilkoff, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French far-right leader Jordan Bardella faces fresh allegations of anti-Semitism</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261126-french-far-right-leader-jordan-bardella-faces-fresh-allegations-of-anti-semitism</link><description>
The leader of France's far-right National Rally party, Jordan #Bardella, is facing fresh accusations of having made anti-Semitic remarks as a teenager. 
 
On Thursday, November 26, French media outlets Mediapart and Le Monde published new excerpts from private Facebook conversations dating back to 2013. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/996304f2-e9c5-11f1-88bd-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/BARDELLA-Miniat.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/996304f2-e9c5-11f1-88bd-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/BARDELLA-Miniat.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2a7c6ede-e9c5-11f1-8209-5360b0ef57c1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:51:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Reporters Without Borders demands suspension of controversial French TV channel CNews</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261126-reporters-without-borders-demands-suspension-controversial-french-tv-channel-cnews</link><description>
Paris-based international press freedom group Reporters Without Borders (RSF) on Thursday called on France's media regulator Arcom to suspend right-wing channel CNews for one month over its failure to uphold pluralism. The news channel owned by conservative billionaire Vincent Bolloré condemned the call for its suspension. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3a179a3c-dbb8-11f1-8811-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6EK9T4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3a179a3c-dbb8-11f1-8811-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6EK9T4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a35c8ac4-e9c4-11f1-8161-1b34202de4d4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:48:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3a179a3c-dbb8-11f1-8811-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6EK9T4.jpg">© Sameer al-Doumy, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Will Spain's far right replace Europe's left-wing stalwart?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261126-will-spain-s-far-right-replace-europe-s-left-wing-stalwart</link><description>
Some 39 million Spaniards will head to the ballot this Sunday to vote in early general elections. Latest polls put the conservative Popular Party ahead of incumbent PM Pedro Sanchez’s Socialists. The third-strongest political force, however, is the far-right Vox party. A strong showing at Sunday’s election could see them form Spain’s next government. FRANCE 24 explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13ac116c-e9b8-11f1-b82e-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-Spain-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13ac116c-e9b8-11f1-b82e-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-Spain-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34c2cfb2-e9b8-11f1-bd33-01df7f3018c8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:51:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Across Africa</category><title>ACROSS AFRICA:  Tunisian Photographer's Family Focus</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/across-africa-tunisian-photographer-s-family-focus-1</link><description>
Stories from the continent with Georja Calvin-Smith. This week, health workers struggling to keep pace with DR Congo's Ebola outbreak say they feel abandoned and unsupported. Also, the World Cup was about more than winning... for some fans, at least. Tunisia's performance may not have been all that its supporters had hoped, but sports photographer Hosni Manoubi is far from negative about a family tradition of documenting his country's international sports showings. [Archive Episode, June 2026]
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d42e595e-e9b3-11f1-9008-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-ebcee408.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d42e595e-e9b3-11f1-9008-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-ebcee408.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0134df40-70a1-11f1-a2d1-bbc19ff962e2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:19:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>In California, exceptional tides and nearly 9m-high waves batter the coast</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261126-in-california-exceptional-tides-and-nearly-9m-high-waves-batter-the-coast</link><description>
USA: Powerful waves and king tides destroyed part of a pier in Pacifica, south of San Francisco, on Wednesday. In Marin County, authorities issued a temporary evacuation order and urged people to stay away from the beach. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3da49d80-e9af-11f1-b62c-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/CALIFORNIA-Minia.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3da49d80-e9af-11f1-b62c-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/CALIFORNIA-Minia.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6775884a-e9af-11f1-9f80-5fc06f4e7cce</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:01:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Spanish economist de Cos to succeed Lagarde as head of ECB</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-spanish-economist-de-cos-succeed-lagarde-head-ecb</link><description>
Spanish monetary economist Pablo Hernandez de Cos on Thursday was set to replace France's Christine Lagarde as the new head of the European Central Bank (ECB). His nomination comes as the Europe's most powerful financial institution grapples with an Iran war-driven resurgence in inflation and a cost of living crisis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8782840e-e9a4-11f1-a5e6-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25290616236227.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8782840e-e9a4-11f1-a5e6-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25290616236227.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c00b4f90-e9a9-11f1-b052-5576e34b99b1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:55:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8782840e-e9a4-11f1-a5e6-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25290616236227.jpg">© Jose Luis Magana, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Lost homes, stolen freedom: National Book Award winners on exile and imprisonment</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261126-lost-homes-stolen-freedom-national-book-award-winners-on-exile-and-imprisonment</link><description>
Two books about losing everything have just won America's most prestigious literary honours. Hannah Lillith Assadi took the National Book Award for fiction for "Paradiso 17", a novel inspired by her late father, who was driven from Palestine in 1948 during the Nakba. Abdelrahman ElGendy won the non-fiction prize for "Huna", his memoir of six years as a political prisoner in Egypt, arrested at 17 alongside his father. ElGendy couldn't be in New York to collect his award: his visa was denied.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faf78374-e9a6-11f1-a42f-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5c1d3af7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faf78374-e9a6-11f1-a42f-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5c1d3af7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">333234c4-e9a6-11f1-8b14-3fb642790777</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:41:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Eve JACKSON</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>How far-right Vox is winning over young voters ahead of Spain's snap election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-how-far-right-vox-winning-over-young-voters-ahead-spain-snap-election</link><description>
Spain's Vox party is winning over many young people ahead of the country's snap election on November 29, particularly men. The far-right party is capitalising on the rising cost of living and anti-immigrant sentiment to expand its once-marginal electoral base. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/714af09c-e8ee-11f1-9f73-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4QF6P2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/714af09c-e8ee-11f1-9f73-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4QF6P2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0269e4aa-e9a0-11f1-97de-138fc9f0a0ac</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:37:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/714af09c-e8ee-11f1-9f73-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4QF6P2.jpg">© Cesar Manso, AFP</source><dc:creator>Barbara GABEL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Across Africa</category><title>Across Africa: The Scars of South Africa's Soweto Uprising</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/across-africa-the-scars-of-south-africa-s-soweto-uprising-1</link><description>
50 years ago, thousands of young South Africans from Soweto protested against apartheid's stranglehold on their education  and the imposition of Afrikaans as a language of instruction. What began as a peaceful protest ended in bloodshed. And men in Northern Benin confront uncomfortable realities about the lives of the women who live and love them.  [Archive edition, June 2026]
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1d4d7f8-e9ac-11f1-9223-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d4bd2670.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1d4d7f8-e9ac-11f1-9223-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d4bd2670.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6307a380-6b22-11f1-b299-cb59d2b33f34</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:28:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category><![CDATA[People & Profit]]></category><title>From leadership crises to tech outages, can corporations rebuild public trust?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261126-from-leadership-crises-to-tech-outages-can-corporations-rebuild-public-trust</link><description>
From cyberattacks to network failures to leadership crises, tech corporations are showing signs of vulnerability. The dramatic resignation and return of Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang has underscored the potential risk of depending on a single leader, both for the company and the entire AI industry. Meanwhile, global outages at Microsoft and a number of US banks have showcased declining public trust in institutions. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ef3a1ca-e988-11f1-87ad-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/PEOPLE-AND-PROFITS-25-11-2026.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ef3a1ca-e988-11f1-87ad-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/PEOPLE-AND-PROFITS-25-11-2026.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">622e0f54-e989-11f1-9ff0-03c4d02edf2f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:55:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Kate MOODY</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French woman on trial for IS group propaganda tells court she’s ‘ashamed’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261126-french-woman-trial-is-group-propaganda-tells-court-she-ashamed</link><description>
The trial of Émilie König, one of France's most high-profile Islamic State (IS) group recruits, opened in a Paris court on Thursday with the 41-year-old mother of five apologising to her children, mother and the "French nation" for her actions. König travelled in 2012 to Syria, where she appeared in the jihadist group's propaganda videos. She was repatriated to France in 2022. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e724ed0-9238-11f0-8810-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/8cea49dc093980a21ecf3652f1db07400c032cf1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e724ed0-9238-11f0-8810-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/8cea49dc093980a21ecf3652f1db07400c032cf1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fadd87d8-e9a3-11f1-a844-6bd7c0817c66</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:48:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e724ed0-9238-11f0-8810-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/8cea49dc093980a21ecf3652f1db07400c032cf1.jpg">© Handout / YPG Press Office/AFP/Archives</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Season's eatings! Celebrating Thanksgiving in France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261126-seasons-eatings-celebrating-thanksgiving-in-france</link><description>
This Thursday marks Thanksgiving in the United States, the biggest travel holiday of the year there and arguably the most important on US calendars. But here in France, it's just another day. However, Americans living in Paris do try to capture the Thanksgiving spirit, though it can be tricky to track down the turkeys and pies required. Joining us to discuss how Americans do Thanksgiving in Paris is Cordon Bleu-trained chef and the owner of Boneshaker Donuts, Amanda Bankert.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a86e1a02-e99a-11f1-9391-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8c006cc1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a86e1a02-e99a-11f1-9391-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8c006cc1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5439fcf2-e996-11f1-918e-1fc28bcfcf9b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:35:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charli James</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Madagascar's near-total abortion ban puts women's lives at risk</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261126-madagascar-s-near-total-abortion-ban-puts-women-s-lives-at-risk</link><description>
November 25 marked the International Day for the Elimination of Violence against Women. Activists argue that tackling gender-based violence also means addressing the wider inequalities that put women at risk, including restrictions on reproductive rights. In Madagascar, abortion is almost entirely banned, even in cases of rape, incest or when a woman's life is at risk. FRANCE 24’s Aurélie Kouman reports on the consequences of the country's strict laws, which force thousands of women to seek unsafe, clandestine procedures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a96bc8ae-e9a0-11f1-a6b9-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-214545-214752-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a96bc8ae-e9a0-11f1-a6b9-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-214545-214752-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ae77c988-e9a0-11f1-b139-8bebe7e3bec9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:22:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Fighting in eastern Congo forces Ebola workers to evacuate, disrupts outbreak response</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261126-fighting-in-eastern-congo-forces-ebola-workers-to-evacuate-disrupts-outbreak-response</link><description>
Escalating fighting in eastern Congo has forced Ebola response workers to leave affected areas and disrupted efforts to contain the deadliest outbreak in the country, health officials and humanitarian workers said Wednesday. Congo’s Ebola outbreak has infected more than 11,700 people and killed more than 5,700 since it was declared in May, according to the latest government data. FRANCE 24's Emmet Livingstone reports from Kinshasa, DR Congo.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e36cb126-e9a0-11f1-aee2-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-215016-215112-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e36cb126-e9a0-11f1-aee2-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-215016-215112-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e8dff794-e9a0-11f1-bc12-9b18ff6e023d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:20:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Moscow drone incursions: Poland to create no-fly zone at Ukraine border</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261126-moscow-drone-incursions-poland-to-create-no-fly-zone-at-ukraine-border</link><description>
Poland will soon create a no-fly zone near the Ukrainian border, a deputy defence minister announced on Wednesday, after several incursions into its airspace it blamed on Russia. Poland backs Ukraine as it fights off Russia's near five-year invasion and has repeatedly accused Moscow of seeking to target Kyiv's supporters with drone incursions and other methods.
